ublk: integrate buffer pools into dispatch and commit paths

Wire ublk_select_buf() into ublk_dispatch_req() and batch dispatch
(__ublk_batch_prep_dispatch) to select a right-sized buffer before
the IO copy. The selected buffer's user_addr is written to iod->addr
so the server sees the buffer address as usual.

Wire ublk_recycle_buf() into __ublk_complete_rq() to return buffers
to their pool after commit. Recycle also happens on dispatch failure
(ublk_start_io returning false).

Update ublk_map_io/ublk_unmap_io to use the buffer pool's user_addr
via ublk_io_buf_addr() helper when BUF_RINGS is active.

Update ublk_setup_iod to skip setting iod->addr when BUF_RINGS is
active (addr is set at dispatch after buffer selection).

Update ublk_check_fetch_buf to allow buf_addr=0 when BUF_RINGS is
active (kernel selects buffers, server must not provide addr).

